# CI, DCO, and ownership

Use this rule when preparing PRs, CI, or release-adjacent checks.

## Local → CI mapping

| Local | Typical CI / workflow |
|---|---|
| `./runtests.sh --ruff` / `--codeformat` | Style/type checks in GitHub Actions (e.g. `pythonapp-*`, setup/CI test workflows) |
| `./runtests.sh --quick --unittests` | Unit test jobs (`cicd_tests.yml`, integration/app workflows) |
| `pre-commit` / `.pre-commit-config.yaml` | Same lint tools as CI |
| Docs build notes in CONTRIBUTING | `build_docs.yml` |

Prefer the smallest local subset that covers touched files before a full matrix.

## DCO

- Every commit must include `Signed-off-by: Name <email>` (Developer Certificate of Origin).
- The GitHub DCO app fails PRs without valid sign-off (`CONTRIBUTING.md` — Signing your work).

## CODEOWNERS

- Review routing is defined in `.github/CODEOWNERS`.
- Kit paths (`.cursor/`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/cursor-kit/`) are owned by the platform team entry there.

**Demo:** open draft PRs against the **fork** default branch only — not upstream.

## Deploy / release (the step after merge)

"Fit the path to production" does not end at a green PR. For a user-facing transform:

- **Document for release:** add a bullet under `## [Unreleased]` -> `### Added` in
  `CHANGELOG.md`. Gate: `bash docs/cursor-kit/scripts/check-changelog.sh <Name> <Named>`.
- **Release train:** merge to default -> nightly (`cron.yml`) / `weekly-preview.yml`
  preview wheels -> tagged release (`release.yml` on `main` + tags) -> NGC bundle
  refresh (`cron-ngc-bundle.yml`).
- **Versioning:** git-tag driven via versioneer (`monai/_version.py`); contributors
  do not hand-edit versions.
- **Docs build:** public API changes are picked up by `build_docs.yml`.

**Source of truth:** `CONTRIBUTING.md` (Signing your work, Submitting pull requests), `.github/CODEOWNERS`, `.github/workflows/release.yml`, `.github/workflows/weekly-preview.yml`, `.github/workflows/cron-ngc-bundle.yml`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`
